) is available as a deduction against any other income for that year of assessment and for any subsequent year of assessment in accordance with section 23;
(
e
)
where the lessor is a leasing company which derives income from onshore leasing as well as from offshore leasing subject to the concessionary rate of tax under section 43F —
(i)
the allowances under section 19, 19A, 20, 21, 22 or 23 in respect of operating leasing must firstly be available as a deduction against the income from such leasing, and any balance of the allowances is available as a deduction against any other income; and
