Assessable income
37.
—(1)  The assessable income of any person from all sources chargeable with tax under this Act for any year of assessment is the remainder of the person’s statutory income for that year after the deductions allowed in this Part have been made.
(2)  For the purposes of this section, unless otherwise provided in this Act or the Economic Expansion Incentives (Relief from Income Tax) Act 1967, where a person is a company whose income (if any) is subject to tax at different rates of tax for any year of assessment, the Comptroller must apportion any sum allowable under subsection (3)(
b
), (
c
), (
d
) or (
