•
Computation rules for determining the amount of income;
•
Special rules for re-characterising or deeming facts or events;
•
Timing rules for the recognition of income or expenses;
•
Tax rates;
•
Tax incentives for economic development;
•
Special rules relating to evidence or documentation; and
•
Rules relating to appeals and dispute resolution.

8.11 The competent authorities of Singapore and its DTA partner are required to
conclude a CAA to settle the mode of application of the mandatory binding
arbitration provisions. Broadly, the CAA will contain the following information:
•
how the request for submission of a case to arbitration is to be made;
•
